.TH VMCTL 1 "2026" "rustbox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vmctl \- command line manager for RustBox virtual machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vmctl
<command> [options]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create NAME [--os windows11|windows10|linux|other] [--iso FILE] [--memory MB] [--cpus N] [--disk-gb N]
Create a VM with defaults tuned for this machine.
.TP
.B list, info, start [--headless], stop [--force], reset, delete
Manage VMs.
.TP
.B snapshot create|list|restore|delete VM [NAME]
Offline disk snapshots.
.TP
.B paravirt VM on|off
Switch disk and NIC to VirtIO after installing the virtio-win drivers in the guest.
.TP
.B iso VM PATH|none
Attach or eject the install ISO.
.TP
.B fetch-drivers
Download the virtio-win driver ISO.
.TP
.B doctor
Verify KVM, QEMU, UEFI firmware and swtpm are available.
.TP
.B host-tune [--apply]
Show or apply host tweaks (KSM, transparent hugepages). Applying requires root.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/rustbox/vms/
holds one directory per VM (vm.toml, disk.qcow2, UEFI variables, TPM state).
.SH SEE ALSO
qemu-system-x86_64(1), qemu-img(1)
